MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

    FailedHealthCheck: Input generation is slow: Hypothesis only generated
    7 valid inputs after 1.16 seconds

and fails `test_extract_timestamp_tzname_zoneinfo_datetime`, the only one of
the four affected tests that carries no `@settings` at all. The health check
is a fixed wall-clock budget on *input generation*; nothing about the
generated inputs, the assertions, or the extension under test is different
here, and the run that tripped it went on to pass every other property.

Suppressing `HealthCheck.too_slow` on exactly the tests that can build a
`ZoneInfo` leaves the deadline and example budget alone, and is a no-op on
hardware fast enough never to trip the check.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [native runner specific]
---
 tests/test_fuzz.py | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/test_fuzz.py b/tests/test_fuzz.py
index 91cd482..7c4f4aa 100644
--- a/tests/test_fuzz.py
+++ b/tests/test_fuzz.py
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ if sys.version_info[:2] == (3, 13) and not sys._is_gil_enabled():
     # Python < 3.14.
     pytest.skip("Hypothesis unavailable", allow_module_level=True)
 
-from hypothesis import assume, given, settings
+from hypothesis import HealthCheck, assume, given, settings
 from hypothesis import strategies as st
 from hypothesis.stateful import RuleBasedStateMachine, invariant, precondition, rule
 
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ def test_travel_to_timestamp(timestamp):
         assert time.time() == expected_ns / NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND
 
 
-@settings(deadline=None)
+@settings(deadline=None, suppress_health_check=[HealthCheck.too_slow])
